<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamburg Stock Exchange</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1558</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Hamburg Exchange, Börse Hamburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> Stock Exchange, founded in 1558, is the oldest exchange in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It began as a meeting place for merchants dealing in goods, bills of exchange and shipping, and helped make Hamburg a leading centre of northern European trade. Its building on the town hall square survived the Great Fire of 1842.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamburg-stock-exchange.jpg" alt="Hamburg Stock Exchange" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staro1 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hh-boerse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
